.TH GITLAB-CI-LOCAL 1 "October 2026" "gitlab-ci-local" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitlab-ci-local \- run GitLab CI pipelines locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitlab-ci-local
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]... [\fIJOB\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitlab-ci-local
parses a
.I .gitlab-ci.yml
pipeline and executes its jobs locally, the same way a GitLab Runner would:
shell jobs run directly on the host, jobs with an
.B image
run in local containers (docker or podman). It expands includes, extends,
references, variables, rules and
.I needs
before execution, and it creates artifacts locally, so pipelines can be
debugged without pushing a single commit.
.PP
If no job is specified, the whole pipeline is executed; otherwise only the
named jobs (and, with
.BR \-\-needs ,
the jobs they need).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show version number.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd \ PATH
Path to a current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-file \ PATH
Location of the
.IR .gitlab\-ci.yml ,
relative to cwd
.RI ( default :
.IR .gitlab\-ci.yml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-home \ PATH
Location of the HOME
.I .gitlab\-ci\-local
folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir \ PATH
Location of the
.I .gitlab\-ci\-local
state dir, relative to cwd.
.TP
.BR \-\-completion
Generate tab completion script (zsh).
.TP
.BR \-\-quiet
Suppress all job output.
.TP
.BR \-\-timestamps
Show timestamps and job duration in the logs.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-job\-name\-padding \ N
Maximum padding for job name (use <= 0 for no padding).
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Enable/disable color output (default: enabled).
.SS Selecting jobs
.TP
.BI \-\-manual \ JOB
One or more manual jobs to run during a pipeline.
.TP
.BR \-\-list
List job information, excluding
.B when:never
jobs.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-all
List job information, including
.B when:never
jobs.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-json
List job information in JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-csv ", " \-\-list\-csv\-all
List job information in CSV format.
.TP
.BR \-\-validate\-dependency\-chain
Validate that jobs needed by, or dependent on, active jobs are also active,
without running anything.
.TP
.BR \-\-needs
Run needed jobs when executing specific jobs.
.TP
.BR \-\-only\-needs
Run needed jobs, except the specified jobs themselves.
.TP
.BI \-\-stage \ STAGE
Run all jobs in a specific stage.
.SS Variables and inputs
.TP
.BI \-\-variable \ KEY=VALUE
Add a variable to all executed jobs. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-unset\-variable \ KEY
Unset a variable. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-input \ KEY=VALUE
Add input to component includes. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-variables\-file \ PATH
Path to the project file variables
.RI ( default :
.IR .gitlab\-ci\-local\-variables.yml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-inputs\-file \ PATH
Path to the component inputs file
.RI ( default :
.IR .gitlab\-ci\-local\-inputs.yml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-variables \ URL
Fetch variables file from a remote location.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignores\-file \ PATH
Path to the ignores file
.RI ( default :
.IR .gitlab\-ci\-local\-ignores ).
.SS Parsing and schema
.TP
.BR \-\-preview
Print the YAML with defaults, includes, extends and references expanded.
.TP
.BR \-\-fetch\-includes
Fetch all external includes one more time.
.TP
.BI \-\-maximum\-includes \ N
The maximum number of includes.
.TP
.BR \-\-json\-schema\-validation ", " \-\-no\-json\-schema\-validation
Enable/disable JSON schema validation (default: enabled).
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore\-schema\-paths \ PATH
JSON schema paths that will be ignored. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore\-predefined\-vars \ VARS
Comma-separated list of predefined pipeline variables for which warnings
should be ignored.
.TP
.BR \-\-evaluate\-rule\-changes ", " \-\-no\-evaluate\-rule\-changes
Whether to evaluate
.B rule:changes
(default: enabled).
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-input\-validation
Skip CI/CD input type, options, and regex validation.
.SS Executors and containers
.TP
.BR \-\-shell\-isolation
Enable artifact isolation for shell-executor jobs.
.TP
.BR \-\-force\-shell\-executor
Force all jobs to be executed using the shell executor (only when the jobs do
not require docker features).
.TP
.BR \-\-shell\-executor\-no\-image
Use the shell executor when no image is specified.
.TP
.BI \-\-default\-image \ IMAGE
Image to use for containers when
.B \-\-shell\-executor\-no\-image=false
and the job has no image.
.TP
.BI \-\-helper\-image \ IMAGE
Image to use for utils containers.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait\-image \ IMAGE
Image to use for the wait container.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait\-for\-services\-timeout \ SECONDS
Timeout for service health checks (default: 30).
.TP
.BR \-\-mount\-cache
Enable docker mount based caching.
.TP
.BR \-\-umask
Set the docker user to 0:0.
.TP
.BI \-\-userns \ MODE
Set the docker executor userns option.
.TP
.BR \-\-privileged
Set the docker executor to privileged mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-device \ DEVICE
Add devices to the docker executor. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-ulimit \ N
Set docker executor ulimit.
.TP
.BI \-\-shm\-size \ SIZE
Set docker executor shared memory size (e.g.\ 256m, 1g).
.TP
.BI \-\-network \ NETWORK
Add networks to the docker executor. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-volume \ VOLUME
Add volumes to the docker executor. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-extra\-host \ HOST
Add extra docker host entries. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-seccomp \ PATH
Set the seccomp profile of containers.
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-file \ PATH
Path to a custom CA certificate file to mount in containers.
.TP
.BI \-\-pull\-policy \ POLICY
Set image pull-policy
.RI ( always " or " if\-not\-present ).
.TP
.BI \-\-container\-executable \ CMD
Command to start the container engine (docker or podman).
.TP
.BI \-\-container\-mac\-address \ MAC
Container MAC address (e.g.\ aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff).
.TP
.BI \-\-container\-emulate \ RUNNER
Emulate a gitlab.com hosted runner (name without architecture).
.TP
.BI \-\-gpus \ IDS
A list of GPU indexes or 'all'.
.TP
.BR \-\-registry
Start a local docker registry and configure containers to use it.
.SS Artifacts and cleanup
.TP
.BR \-\-artifacts\-to\-source
Copy the generated artifacts into cwd.
.TP
.BR \-\-cleanup
Remove docker resources after they have been used.
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrency \ N
Limit the number of jobs that run simultaneously.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every option can be set by default through the corresponding environment
variable, prefixed with
.B GCL_
and upper-cased, e.g.\ \fBGCL_NEEDS=true\fR for \fB\-\-needs\fR.
Alternatively, defaults can be placed in
.I .gitlab\-ci\-local\-env
in the working directory, or in
.IR $HOME/.gitlab\-ci\-local/.env .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .gitlab\-ci.yml
The pipeline definition executed in the current directory.
.TP
.I $HOME/.gitlab\-ci\-local/
Per-user state: remote and home file variables, cached remote includes.
.TP
.I .gitlab\-ci\-local/
Project state dir: cached remote includes, job artifacts and logs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List the jobs of the pipeline in the current git repository:
.B gitlab\-ci\-local \-\-list
.TP
Run the whole pipeline:
.B gitlab\-ci\-local
.TP
Run a single job and the jobs it needs:
.B gitlab\-ci\-local \-\-needs \-\-stage=build \-j build\-job
.TP
Print the fully expanded pipeline YAML:
.B gitlab\-ci\-local \-\-preview
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/firecow/gitlab-ci-local
.UE
